u&#34;, &#34;eightfolddemo-mike.com&#34;, &#34;nab-sandbox.com.au&#34;], &#34;backoff Variables&#34;: {&#34;notification Keys To Backoff&#34;: [&#34;position_notification&#34;], &#34;backoff Multiplier&#34;: 2, &#34;backoff Unengage Num Days Threshold&#34;: 14, &#34;minimum Notif Count Before Backoff&#34;: 3, &#34;lack Of Sends Backoff Enabled&#34;: true, &#34;engagement Backoff Enabled&#34;: true}, &#34;accelerate Variables&#34;: {&#34;notification Keys To Accelerate&#34;: [], &#34;accelerate Multiplier&#34;: 0.5}, &#34;batch User Notifications Db Get&#34;: true, &#34;scheduler Op Batch Size&#34;: 1000}}}, &#34;onboarding Data&#34;: {}, &#34;ip Geolocation&#34;: &#34;Kolkata, West Bengal, IN&#34;, &#34;ip Geolocation Lat Long&#34;: &#34;22.518,88.3832&#34;, &#34;theme Builder User&#34;: null, &#34;instance Banner Data&#34;: {&#34;display Banner&#34;: false, &#34;display Text&#34;: &#34;&#34;}} Drive Digital mixed Signal Verification of Complex Signal processing IPs and chips<br><br><font color="#2a9b91"><font size="4px"><b>Your Role</b></font><br><br>Key responsibilities in your new role</font><br><ul> <li>Drive Digital mixed Signal Verification of Complex Signal processing IPs and chips</li> <li>Enable AI in Verification</li> <li>Technical guidance and career mentorship to the team</li> <li>Lead from the front</li> <li>Hands-on experience building Simulink models that correlate to fixed-point hardware implementations (bit-accurate or tolerance-defined reference models).</li> <li>Experience collaborating with RTL design and DV teams (UVM/scoreboards/reference models), driving requirements-to-implementation traceability.</li> <li>Ability to interpret and integrate analog collateral (ADC behaviour, trims/calibration, validity timing, comparators/monitors) into digital models and verification plans.</li> <li>Strong system-thinking and ownership mindset; comfortable leading cross-team technical decisions and driving signoff-quality closure.</li> <li>Power converter control experience (multi-phase regulation, current sharing, transient optimization) is highly desired</li> <li>Mixed-signal verification exposure (co-simulation workflows, model correlation).</li></ul><br><br><font color="#2a9b91"><font size="4px"><b>Your Profile</b></font><br><br>Qualifications and skills to help you succeed<br></font><br><ul><li>System modelling & specification: Build end-to-end behavioural models (plant + sensing + digital control + telemetry), define measurable requirements (stability, transient response, accuracy, latency), and translate them into implementable specs.</li><li>Filter/algorithm implementation alignment: Own the modelling and fixed-point specification of key digital signal-processing elements (moving averages, programmable IIR poles/compensators, notch/CIC-style filters, envelope/marker capture, scaling/formatting), and work with RTL designers to ensure faithful implementation.</li><li>Strong background in discrete-time filter design and fixed-point DSP implementation (IIR/PID, rounding/saturation behaviour, coefficient quantization, numeric stability).</li><li>Cross-functional integration: Act as the technical interface between analog and digital teams; Define analog collateral (ADC behaviour, sampling/validity timing, trims/calibration, comparators/monitors) and ensure consistent assumptions in models, RTL, and verification.</li><li>Verification strategy & closure: Define multi-level verification strategy (math-block golden models → subsystem digital verification →mixed-signal validation → full-chip end-to-end scenarios) and drive closure with verification leads.</li><li>Bring-up & debug readiness: Define bring-up checklists, debug observability requirements, and lab validation plans; support root-cause analysis across RTL, firmware, and bench data.</li><li>Documentation & leadership: Own technical collateral (architecture, modelling assumptions, coefficient derivations, fixed-point formats, test plans) and lead design/verification reviews.</li></ul><br><br><br><strong>Contact:</strong><br> Vidhi Ashok.Thakkar@infineon.com<br><br><p><b>#We Are In for driving decarbonization and digitalization.</b><br>As a global leader in semiconductor solutions in power systems and Io T, Infineon enables game-changing solutions for green and efficient energy, clean and safe mobility, as well as smart and secure Io T. Together, we drive innovation and customer success, while caring for our people and empowering them to reach ambitious goals. Be a part of making life easier, safer and greener.<br><b>Are you in?</b><b><br></b><br><strong style="background-color: initial;">We are on a journey to create the best Infineon for everyone.<br></strong>This means we embrace diversity and inclusion and welcome everyone for who they are. At Infineon, we offer a working environment characterized by trust, openness, respect and tolerance and are committed to give all applicants and employees equal opportunities. We base our recruiting decisions on the applicant´s experience and skills. <a href="https://www.infineon.com/cms/en/about-infineon/company/contacts/">Learn more</a> about our various contact channels.<br>Please let your recruiter know if they need to pay special attention to something in order to enable your participation in the interview process.<br><a href="https://www.infineon.com/cms/en/careers/diversity-and-inclusion/">Click here</a> for more information about Diversity & Inclusion at Infineon.</p> requirements-to-implementation traceability. Ability to interpret and integrate analog collateral (ADC behaviour, trims/calibration, validity timing, comparators/monitors) into digital models and verification plans. Strong system-thinking and ownership mindset; comfortable leading cross-team technical decisions and driving signoff-quality closure. Power converter control experience (multi-phase regulation, current sharing, transient optimization) is highly desired Mixed-signal verification exposure (co-simulation workflows, model correlation). System modelling & specification: Build end-to-end behavioural models (plant + sensing + digital control + telemetry), define measurable requirements (stability, transient response, accuracy, latency), and translate them into implementable specs. Filter/algorithm implementation alignment: Own the modelling and fixed-point specification of key digital signal-processing elements (moving averages, programmable IIR poles/compensators, notch/CIC-style filters, envelope/marker capture, scaling/formatting), and work with RTL designers to ensure faithful implementation. Strong background in discrete-time filter design and fixed-point DSP implementation (IIR/PID, rounding/saturation behaviour, coefficient quantization, numeric stability). Cross-functional integration: Act as the technical interface between analog and digital teams; Define analog collateral (ADC behaviour, sampling/validity timing, trims/calibration, comparators/monitors) and ensure consistent assumptions in models, RTL, and verification. Verification strategy & closure: Define multi-level verification strategy (math-block golden models → subsystem digital verification →mixed-signal validation → full-chip end-to-end scenarios) and drive closure with verification leads. Bring-up & debug readiness: Define bring-up checklists, debug observability requirements, and lab validation plans; support root-cause analysis across RTL, firmware, and bench data. Documentation & leadership: Own technical collateral (architecture, modelling assumptions, coefficient derivations, fixed-point formats, test plans) and lead design/verification reviews. We are on a journey to create the best Infineon for everyone. This means we embrace diversity and inclusion and welcome everyone for who they are. At Infineon, we offer a working environment characterized by trust, openness, respect and tolerance and are committed to give all applicants and employees equal opportunities. We base our recruiting decisions on the applicant´s experience and skills. Job description&#34;, &#34;show Insights Widget&#34;: true}, {&#34;id&#34;: &#34;company&#34;, &#34;sections&#34;: [&#34;perks&#34;, &#34;position_custom_content&#34;, &#34;videos&#34;, &#34;blogs&#34;], &#34;label&#34;: &#34;Company and benefits&#34;, &#34;show Insights Widget&#34;: false}], &#34;sections Config&#34;: {&#34;perks&#34;: {&#34;items&#34;: [{&#34;title&#34;: &#34;Career development & learning&#34;, &#34;description&#34;: &#34;About 17,000 free Linked In Learning courses in 10 languages, Mentoring & Coaching programs, Global Onboarding process as well as Virtual & f2f trainings&#34;, &#34;image&#34;: &#34;https://static.vscdn.net/images/careers/demo/infineon/1760510028::Graduation+Cap+Benefits+XS&#34;, &#34;image Alt&#34;: null, &#34;icon&#34;: &#34;fa-graduation-cap&#34;, &#34;is Favicon&#34;: true}, {&#34;title&#34;: &#34;Time & flexibility&#34;, &#34;description&#34;: &#34;Flexible working hours & part-time work, Mobile work (specifications based on job profile and local requirements), Remote work from abroad / Workation (EU), Sabbatical (EU)&#34;, &#34;image&#34;: &#34;https://static.vscdn.net/images/careers/demo/infineon/1760510085::Business+Time+Benefits+XS&#34;, &#34;image Alt&#34;: null, &#34;icon&#34;: &#34;fa-user-clock&#34;, &#34;is Favicon&#34;: true}, {&#34;title&#34;: &#34;Health & wellbeing&#34;, &#34;description&#34;: &#34;Health activities & programs, Health & Well-being Linked In Learning Journey,Health & Well-being Community&#34;, &#34;image&#34;: &#34;https://static.vscdn.net/images/careers/demo/infineon/1760510145::User+Doctor+Benefits+XS&#34;, &#34;image Alt&#34;: null, &#34;icon&#34;: &#34;fa-user-md&#34;, &#34;is Favicon&#34;: true}, {&#34;title&#34;: &#34;Your working environment&#34;, &#34;description&#34;: &#34;Employee events, Open & global community e.g. cross-site exchange through the virtuality of all meetings, Open office spaces&#34;, &#34;image&#34;: &#34;https://static.vscdn.n