e faithful implementation. Strong background in discrete-time filter design and fixed-point DSP implementation (IIR/PID, rounding/saturation behaviour, coefficient quantization, numeric stability). Cross-functional integration: Act as the technical interface between analog and digital teams; Define analog collateral (ADC behaviour, sampling/validity timing, trims/calibration, comparators/monitors) and ensure consistent assumptions in models, RTL, and verification. Verification strategy & closure: Define multi-level verification strategy (math-block golden models → subsystem digital verification →mixed-signal validation → full-chip end-to-end scenarios) and drive closure with verification leads. Bring-up & debug readiness: Define bring-up checklists, debug observability requirements, and lab validation plans; support root-cause analysis across RTL, firmware, and bench data. Documentation & leadership: Own technical collateral (architecture, modelling assumptions, coefficient derivations, fixed-point formats, test plans) and lead design/verification reviews. We are on a journey to create the best Infineon for everyone. This means we embrace diversity and inclusion and welcome everyone for who they are. At Infineon, we offer a working environment characterized by trust, openness, respect and tolerance and are committed to give all applicants and employees equal opportunities. We base our recruiting decisions on the applicant´s experience and skills. Job description Benefits and company information Job Id HRC1636968 Job Family Research & Development Duration of Employment Permanent Workplace Type Hybrid Join as Management Drive Digital mixed Signal Verification of Complex Signal processing IPs and chips Your Role Key responsibilities in your new role Drive Digital mixed Signal Verification of Complex Signal processing IPs and chips Enable AI in Verification Technical guidance and career mentorship to the team Lead from the front Hands-on experience building Simulink models that correlate to fixed-point hardware implementations (bit-accurate or tolerance-defined reference models). Experience collaborating with RTL design and DV teams (UVM/scoreboards/reference models), driving requirements-to-implementation traceability. Ability to interpret and integrate analog collateral (ADC behaviour, trims/calibration, validity timing, comparators/monitors) into digital models and verification plans. Strong system-thinking and ownership mindset; comfortable leading cross-team technical decisions and driving signoff-quality closure. Power converter control experience (multi-phase regulation, current sharing, transient optimization) is highly desired Mixed-signal verification exposure (co-simulation workflows, model correlation). Your Profile Qualifications and skills to help you succeed System modelling & specification: Build end-to-end behavioural models (plant + sensing + digital control + telemetry), define measurable requirements (stability, transient response, accuracy, latency), and translate them into implementable specs. Filter/algorithm implementation alignment: Own the modelling and fixed-point specification of key digital signal-processing elements (moving averages, programmable IIR poles/compensators, notch/CIC-style filters, envelope/marker capture, scaling/formatting), and work with RTL designers to ensure faithful implementation. Strong background in discrete-time filter design and fixed-point DSP implementation (IIR/PID, rounding/saturation behaviour, coefficient quantization, numeric stability). Cross-functional integration: Act as the technical interface between analog and digital teams; Define analog collateral (ADC behaviour, sampling/validity timing, trims/calibration, comparators/monitors) and ensure consistent assumptions in models, RTL, and verification. Verification strategy & closure: Define multi-level verification strategy (math-block golden models → subsystem digital verification →mixed-signal validation → full-chip