ailto: r-ifx-tnamericas@infineon.com' target='_blank'>Americas Talent Acquisition</a>&#34;}, {&#34;type&#34;: &#34;instruction&#34;, &#34;label&#34;: &#34;Form CC-305 <br> OMB Control Number 1250-0005 <br> Expires 1/31/2020 <br><br> <b>Why are you being asked to complete this form?</b> <br> Because we do business with the government, we must reach out to, hire, and provide equal opportunity to qualified people with disabilities. (Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended. For more information about this form or the equal employment obligations of Federal contractors, visit the U.S. Department of Labor's Office of Federal Contract Compliance Programs website at www.dol.gov/ofccp. PUBLIC BURDEN STATEMENT: According to the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995 no persons are required to respond to a collection of information unless such collection displays a valid OMB control number.) To help us measure how well we are doing, we are asking you tell us if you have a disability or if you ever had a disability. Completing this form is voluntary, but we hope that you will choose to fill it out. If you are applying for a job, any answer you give will be kept private and will not be used against you in any way. If you already work for us, your answer will not be used against you in any way. Because a person may become disabled at any time, we are required to ask all of our employees to update their information every five years. You may voluntarily self-identify as having a disability on this form without fear of any punishment because you did not identify as having a disability earlier. <br> <br> <b>How do I know if I have a disability?</b> <br>You are considered to have a disability if you have a physical or mental impairment or medical condition that substantially limits a major life activity, or if you have a history or record of such an impairment or medical condition. <br> <br> <b>Disabilities include, but are not limited to:</b> <br> • Blindness <br> • Autism <br> • Bipolar disorder <br> • Post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) <br> • Deafness <br> • Cerebral palsy <br> • Major depression <br> • Obsessive compulsive disorder <br> • Cancer <br> • HIV/AIDS <br> • Multiple sclerosis (MS) <br> • Impairments requiring the use of a wheelchair <br> • Diabetes <br> • Schizophrenia <br> • Missing limbs or partially missing limbs <br> • Intellectual disability (previously called mental retardation) <br> • Epilepsy <br> • Muscular dystrophy&#34;}, {&#34;choices&#34;: [{&#34;value&#34;: &#34;EEOCDisability_Y&#34;, &#34;label&#34;: &#34;Yes, I have a disability (or previously had a disability)&#34;}, {&#34;value&#34;: &#34;EEOCDisability_N&#34;, &#34;label&#34;: &#34;No, I don't have a disability&#34;}, {&#34;value&#34;: &#34;EEOCDisability_NA&#34;, &#34;label&#34;: &#34;Decline to answer&#34;}], &#34;type&#34;: &#34;dropdown&#34;, &#34;label&#34;: &#34;Disability&#34;, &#34;question Id&#34;: &#34;[Applicant.EEOCDisability]&#34;, &#34;choices Sort Order&#34;: &#34;ascending&#34;, &#34;required&#34;: false}, {&#34;type&#34;: &#34;instruction&#34;, &#34;label&#34;: &#34;I understand that in connection with the application process, Infineon Technologies Americas Corp. (the “ Company”) may check the official publication of restricted parties in the Federal Register and/or the official lists of restricted parties maintained on the websites of the Departments of Commerce, State, and Treasury to ensure full compliance with all of the terms and conditions of the restrictions placed on the parties on these lists.<br><br> I also understand that in connection with the application process, the Company may check the INTERPOL Criminal Information System of Notices that contains personal information and criminal history, including international alerts for fugitives, suspected criminals, persons linked to or of interest in an ongoing criminal investigation, persons and entities subject to UN Security Council Sanctions, potential threats, missing persons, and deceased persons.<br><br> I understand that the information contained in the restricted parties lists maintained by the United States government and the INTERPOL Criminal Information System may be used in whole or in part for the purpose of evaluating me for employment.<br><br> I hereby authorize the Company to check the restricted parties lists maintained by the United States government and the INTERPOL Criminal Information System as part of my application process.<br><br> I understand and agree that any employment relationship entered into between Infineon Technologies Americas Corp. and me is predicated on the truthfulness of the statements made in this application and resume submitted, as well as interviews. Any falsification or omission may result in rejection of the application or termination of employment at any time during my employment, if hired.<br><br> I also understand that completion of this application is in no way to be construed as a guarantee of employment at Infineon Technologies Corp. The employment relationship is at-will and can be terminated, with or without cause, at any time by the company or the employee, with or without notice.<br><br> I give the Employer the right to investigate all references and to secure additional information about me, if job related. I hereby release the Employer and its Representatives from liability for seeking such information.&#34;}], &#34;title&#34;: &#34;Additional Personal Information (US-specific)&#34;}, {&#34;countries&#34;: [&#34;SG&#34;], &#34;questions&#34;: [{&#34;choices&#34;: [{&#34;value&#34;: 38998666, &#34;label&#34;: &#34;Singapore Citizen&#34;}, {&#34;value&#34;: 38998667, &#34;label&#34;: &#34;Singapore Permanent Resident&#34;}, {&#34;value&#34;: 38998668, &#34;label&#34;: &#34;Others&#34;}], &#34;label&#34;: &#34;Identity Type&#34;, &#34;question Id&#34;: &#34;[Empfaenger.Benutzerdefiniert Liste Stammdaten2]&#34;, &#34;type&#34;: &#34;dropdown&#34;, &#34;required&#34;: true}, {&#34;type